le workstation  you can imagine a situation where users  would go ahead they would prep their  samples  they would set the tray into the  instrument run through the study manager  workflow  walk away because we're doing automated  data analysis  and uh reporting and their colleague  would be able to  walk up shortly afterwards with their  prep samples  submit their uh  samples as well into the study manager  software and walk away and as soon as  the first one finishes the second one  would start  and that increases their labor  utilization rate because they'd be able  to do other things there too  again it allows the entire sample sets  to be submitted for acquisition prior to  the completion of other batches so  that's where  batch q submission really fits in as  well  um some other features it has is the  ability to do work list and work  workless  import workflows so the study manager  software permits a user to submit sample  sets from existing mass on our work list  if you can think about the work list  that would have been created perhaps  during the validation period or maybe  even the development period if those are  already in place in your lab on the  workstation  the routine analysis uh or the routine  analyst would be able to select those  work lists  from the drop down and be able to submit  them or  if you have an import file so for  example from a spreadsheet uh which  could come from an lis  or a limb system there too they would be  able to import those samples as well  using a drop-down map file which would  then translate all the files into a work  list there too and that would all be set  up so that the routine analyst would  again just have to do simple drop downs  and move through the entire software  program is really designed around  improving the productivity and limiting  the steps to  from sample submission to reporting  finally  one of the other features that it has is  the ability to import and export data to  an lis and a limb system so as you can  see in the illustration off to the right  there on the screen  not only are you able to pull work lists  for example from an lis but you'd  actually be able to submit it  analyze it report it and then upload  those results  back up into your lis there too into a  report that's specific for  the type of essay that you're running  there as well so it can be configured to  both  export and upload the results into the  lis system as well as import for them so  it really makes for a very complete full  circle  workflow and able to work through  so those are the benefits um i'd like to  walk through before we go into the  question answer and just do a quick  demonstration now these are actually um  screenshots obviously from the system  i can't do a webinar with a live system  but um this was all done on a system as  well so it's effectively a live  demonstration  and what you're looking at right here is  a a  shot of a workstation that we have the  study manager program is which again is  included in all of the agilent lcms  triple quads  has been set up and configured as an  icon and a routine analyst or a medical  technologist  would be able to simply double click on  the  icon to launch the study manager  software and would  uh simply select a study from that as  well as i mentioned we  talked about work list and work list  import  types of studies there are a few others  but they're a little bit outside of the  scope of this as well  that said your your application engineer  or your uh  representative would be able to walk you  through those as well and give you some  more details but again here in this  example we're just going to do a simple  work list  only selection again  you would select the appropriate file  and work list from the drop downs that  are on the right  uh this particular work list is called a  demo work list  you can put some specific information  for traceability so for example if you  wanted to  label the the sample set with a lot  